           RetroForth & nga 2026.x Release Notes

================================================================

- general

- building

  - add build profile support
  - more modular compilation of nga-c

- toolchain

  - retro-muri gained additional directives
  - retro-muri now validates instruction bundles
  - update retro-muri.py to match functionality of the C
  - added retro-muri.js (node)
  - generate-layout to turn a description of dictionary and
    image format into usable includes for the VM & tools
  - small cleanups in glossary.retro

- documentation

  - update man pages
  - fix typos in glossary
  - remove words from glossary which are no longer in retro
  - fix typos across manual

- examples

- image

  - use new D directive to build initial dictionary
  - fill in missing `d:source` data
  - reduce use of magic numbers
  - konilo vocabulary alignment:
    - add: `n:add`
           `n:sub`
           `n:mul`
           `n:div`
           `n:mod`
           `n:divmod`
           `shift-left`
           `shift-right`

- library
  - remove konilo words that are now part of the core image

- retro-compiler

  - removed retro-compiler

- new minimal nga implementations

  - common lisp (sbcl)
  - scheme (chicken)
  - javascript (node)
  - java
  - kotlin
  - haskell (ghc)

- nga-c

  - add device range validation for i/o
  - add checks for file i/o operations
  - split string handling to a separate source file
  - split scripting interface to a separate source file
  - split nga core into separate nga_core.c
  - better compile time error messages if device/module order
    is incorrect
  - remove unused code
  - clean up and consolidate duplicated utf8/32 code
  - cleaner handling of included files via the scripting
    interface
  - work on making the device registrations more robust
  - support building a retro-runtime(1) without embedded image
  - fix bugs
    - rng ignored failures on opening/reading /dev/urandom
    - prefer use of host-specific random functions where
      possible
    - read_line() in the scripting interface could mishandle a
      multibyte character at the start of a line
    - scripting_arg() indexes sys_argv[a + 2] with no bounds
      check
    - i_fe and i_st index VM memory directly with unvalidated
      guest addresses
    - jump/call targets can drive ip negative
    - the fast execution path reads an opcode through
      (uint8_t *)&opcode, which depends on host byte order
    - terminal setup ignores tcgetattr, tcsetattr, and ioctl
      failures
    - sockets creation could return an ambiguos handle
    - sockets failures were not detected correctly
  - evaluate() truncates by writing into the caller's buffer.
    Use a local TIB-sized buffer instead.

- nga-x11

  - moved to separate directory from nga-c

